 "lines": {
  "When you’re ready, tap Finish & save.": "2cdd103ec4bc",
  "StoryPrints tells you how many photos it will save and where.": "2a4083636254",
  "Photos still to crop aren’t saved, so go back with Continue the session if you missed any.": "8cb0106c72bd",
  "Tap Save. Your photos go to the gallery with their descriptions and dates, and you’re ready to start again.": "893df41120f1",
  "StoryPrints always saves new copies.": "0d2bf9b11dec",
  "The photos you added are never changed.": "f6c8d3a34c75",
  "When you’re happy, you can delete the originals yourself, or keep them, for example to take more photos from an album page later.": "a445eaf78e8f",
  "The description and date are saved inside each new photo.": "e449b08df718",
  "To keep them in a folder of their own, tap Choose folder": "163077355fc0",
  "and pick or make one inside Pictures or DCIM.": "354bd01e962e",
  "StoryPrints remembers it for next time.": "54401657628a",
  "Save to the photo gallery instead switches back.": "6c08c7e5f4b5",
  "To stop part way, tap Save progress.": "aaa9d22e95d2",
  "Give the work a name and choose a folder for it, such as a StoryPrints folder in Pictures.": "8bf614b42e4b",
  "The photos that are ready are saved there, and everything else is kept beside them.": "ba1beba5ce7c",
  "Next time, tap Continue under Continue saved work.": "e58dd5140732"
 }
